def i2c-pullups (t_rise = 1 us, c_bus = 400 pF)
  title "I2C pull-up pair"
  about "One 4.7 kΩ pull-up on SDA and one on SCL to the bus supply: the value for 100 kHz on a small board
      (REQ.missing). For Fast mode (400 kHz) 2.2 kΩ."
  port sda "the SDA net"
  port scl "the SCL net"
  port vcc "the bus supply (the lower one when the devices run from different supplies)"
  part R1 resistor 0805W8F4701T5E lcsc C17673 value 4.7k "{as}: SDA pull-up 4.7 k"
  part R2 resistor 0805W8F4701T5E lcsc C17673 value 4.7k "{as}: SCL pull-up 4.7 k"
  net sda @vcc R1.2 bus i2c
  net scl @vcc R2.2 bus i2c
  net vcc R1.1 R2.1
  derive R1.value pullup(v = vcc, t_rise = t_rise, c_bus = c_bus)
  derive R2.value pullup(v = vcc, t_rise = t_rise, c_bus = c_bus)
  covers REQ.missing REQ.value
  notes "Once per bus. Modules often bring their own pull-ups (\"pull\": \"up\" with \"pull_ohm\" on their pins);
      parallel pull-ups lower the value, and REQ.missing adds them up."
  notes "The block marks both nets with \"bus\": \"i2c\", so that REQ.missing checks them even when the MCU's pins are
      called GP4/GP5."
